From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: restart domain after failed NHI suspend

tb_domain_suspend_noirq() stops the control channel before the platform NHI
suspend operation runs. The PM core does not resume a device when its own
suspend callback fails.

A platform mailbox timeout therefore leaves the control channel stopped.
Later ICM commands fail, and domain rescans cannot recover the controller.

Restart the domain control channel before returning the platform error. This
restores the state changed earlier in the same callback.

Signed-off-by: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
@@ -974,20 +974,30 @@
 
 static int __nhi_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev, bool wakeup)
 {
 	struct tb *tb = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct tb_nhi *nhi = tb->nhi;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, resume_ret;
 
 	ret = tb_domain_suspend_noirq(tb);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
 	if (nhi->ops->suspend_noirq) {
 		ret = nhi->ops->suspend_noirq(tb->nhi, wakeup);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The PM core does not call resume_noirq() for the device
+			 * whose suspend callback failed. Restart the domain control
+			 * channel that tb_domain_suspend_noirq() already stopped.
+			 */
+			resume_ret = tb_domain_resume_noirq(tb);
+			if (resume_ret)
+				dev_warn(dev, "failed to restart domain after aborted suspend: %d\n",
+					 resume_ret);
 			return ret;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
 

